{
  "_comment": [
    "The ONLY place provider knowledge lives. Skill prose must never carry a model id,",
    "endpoint or price -- see cli/README.md.",
    "",
    "A model has one or more ROUTES, tried in order. A route is the same underlying model",
    "at a different reseller. Failing over from minimax-h3 to seedance would silently",
    "change the film, so a different model is a different entry here, never a fallback.",
    "",
    "`input` is the route's REAL request contract captured from its own doc page: required",
    "fields, defaults, types and per-role reference field names. Providers disagree in ways",
    "that fail at submit -- kie's wan wants duration as a string, seedance as an integer;",
    "wavespeed puts the model in the URL path and has no `input` wrapper at all.",
    "",
    "`schemaVerified:false` means the contract is still a guess and the CLI says so before",
    "spending. `verified:false` means no job has ever succeeded on that route.",
    "`measuredCredits` is a FACT from a real job (see runs/.ledger.jsonl); `priceUsd` is an",
    "estimate.",
    "",
    "Measured 2026-09-10 on kie: seedream-5-pro basic 1:1 = 7 credits; seedance-2-fast",
    "4s/480p/16:9 = 46.8 credits, returned 864x496 @24fps with native audio. Video is ~7x",
    "an image there, so budget in credits rather than in the USD guesses.",
    "WaveSpeed's docs describe outputs as { video: url }; the live API returns outputs as an ARRAY of urls. extractUrls is deliberately liberal and absorbed the difference -- do not tighten it to a documented shape."
  ],
  "captured": "2026-09-10",
  "staleAfterDays": 30,
  "providers": {
    "kie": {
      "label": "kie.ai",
      "baseUrl": "https://api.kie.ai",
      "keyEnv": "KIE_API_KEY",
      "keyFile": ".config/kie/key",
      "signup": "https://kie.ai/api-key",
      "errorInBody": true,
      "bodyOkCode": 200,
      "credits": "/api/v1/chat/credit",
      "creditUnit": "credits",
      "upload": {
        "host": "https://kieai.redpandaai.co",
        "base64": "/api/file-base64-upload",
        "stream": "/api/file-stream-upload"
      },
      "families": {
        "jobs": {
          "create": "/api/v1/jobs/createTask",
          "query": "/api/v1/jobs/recordInfo",
          "queryParam": "taskId",
          "bodyShape": "wrapped",
          "note": "{ model, input, callBackUrl }. Errors arrive as HTTP 200 with body code 500."
        },
        "veo": {
          "create": "/api/v1/veo/generate",
          "query": "/api/v1/veo/record-info",
          "queryParam": "taskId",
          "bodyShape": "flat"
        }
      }
    },
    "wavespeed": {
      "label": "WaveSpeed",
      "baseUrl": "https://api.wavespeed.ai",
      "keyEnv": "WAVESPEED_API_KEY",
      "keyFile": ".config/wavespeed/key",
      "signup": "https://wavespeed.ai",
      "errorInBody": false,
      "credits": null,
      "creditUnit": null,
      "upload": null,
      "families": {
        "v3": {
          "create": "/api/v3/{model}",
          "query": "/api/v3/predictions/{id}/result",
          "modelInPath": true,
          "idInPath": true,
          "bodyShape": "bare",
          "note": "Model is the URL path; the body IS the input object. Errors use HTTP status. Their docs warn against blindly retrying a POST -- a disconnected response may still be an accepted prediction, which is exactly the exit-5 rule."
        }
      }
    }
  },
